      "date": "2026-05-09T20:17:01.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS exceeds analyst expectations while revenues lag behind",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹21.71 (up from ₹17.88 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹69.5b (up 5.9% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹3.58b (up 22% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 5.1% (up from 4.5% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue missed analyst estimates by 2.4%. Earnings per share (EPS) exceeded analyst estimates by 1.9%. Revenue is forecast to grow 12% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, compared to a 12% growth forecast for the Metals and Mining industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has fallen by 10% per year but the company’s share price has only fallen by 1% per year, which means it has not declined as severely as earnings.",
